What is a Power Supply Unit for AI Data Centers?
A Power Supply Unit (PSU) for AI data centers represents a specialized class of electrical infrastructure designed to meet the extreme energy requirements of artificial intelligence workloads. Unlike conventional data center power supplies, these units are engineered to deliver stable, high-capacity DC power to GPU clusters and AI accelerators while maintaining exceptional efficiency—often exceeding 98% in premium models.
These systems incorporate multiple innovative features critical for AI operations: advanced thermal management to handle concentrated heat loads, redundant power pathways ensuring uninterrupted operation, and intelligent monitoring capabilities that track power quality in real-time. Manufacturers are increasingly adopting next-generation materials like gallium nitride (GaN) semiconductors to enhance power density and energy efficiency.
